  {
    "description": "Store, change or retire a memory by sending a proposal of ops. To store something new use op `add` (a `kind` and its `fields`; the schema lists them). `revise`, `supersede` and `retract` (and `link`, `annotate` in the full profile) act on memories that already exist: use ids from recall or an earlier result, never an invented one. Cite what the user said as `evidence: [{\"quote\": ...}]`. The proposal is validated, then committed or held for review: say it is saved only when `status` is `committed` (`pending` means a human must approve). Read the findings: a duplicate warning usually means supersede; an unscoped warning means `revise` that memory, not add it again. Side effects: a proposal is recorded; if the policy commits it, memories are added or superseded or retracted (history is kept). Memories go to your own space; `space: global` writes to the shared memory and needs permission.",
    "input_schema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "proposal": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "The proposal of the `lite` MCP profile: only the ops an agent needs to write and correct\nmemory (`add`, `revise`, `supersede`, `retract`). `link` and `annotate` are left out: a weak\ntool-caller reaches for `annotate` as the easy way to \"note\" something and stores nothing.",
          "properties": {
            "idempotency_key": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "default": null
            },
            "note": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "default": null
            },
            "ops": {
              "items": {
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "description": "Create a NEW memory (item + first revision). This is how anything gets stored: pick the\n`kind` and give its `fields`. Say where it applies (`scope: universal`, or `anchors` /\n`about`), or a directive is flagged as unscoped.",
                    "properties": {
                      "derived_from": {
                        "default": [],
                        "items": {
                          "anyOf": [
                            {
                              "type": "string"
                            },
                            {
                              "description": "A record id as `table:id`.",
                              "examples": [
                                "memory:0194f3a1b2c3d4e5f6a7"
                              ],
                              "type": "string"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        "type": "array"
                      },
                      "evidence": {
                        "default": [],
                        "items": {
                          "additionalProperties": false,
                          "description": "What a memory comes from: words that were said, found in the episode log.\n\nGive a `quote` and the daemon looks it up among your recent episodes (it must occur there\nliterally, case and spacing aside); nothing is stored when it does not. Give an `episode`\nid as well to name the exact message; the quote must then occur in that one.",
                          "properties": {
                            "episode": {
                              "anyOf": [
                                {
                                  "description": "A record id as `table:id`.",
                                  "examples": [
                                    "memory:0194f3a1b2c3d4e5f6a7"
                                  ],
                                  "type": "string"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "null"
                                }
                              ],
                              "default": null,
                              "description": "Optional: the episode id, when you know it."
                            },
                            "quote": {
                              "anyOf": [
                                {
                                  "type": "string"
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "null"
                                }
                              ],
                              "default": null,
                              "description": "Words from the conversation, copied literally (a sentence)."
                            }
                          },
                          "type": "object"
                        },
                        "type": "array"
                      },
                      "fields": {
                        "additionalProperties": true,
